domain ADR0035:
  description "ADR-0035 revision 2 proposal: resolve character revision scope from the owner's request."

problem P1:
  |
    The accepted character requirements freeze each revision's resolved change scope,
    but the ordinary natural-language command has no scope-resolution step. The
    existing appearance path is selected only by a test-only buildRoutes option.

evidence E1:
  |
    Character requirement v5 R2/R3 protects the requested revision scope and lets
    the owner's request outrank old V3 only within its resolved scope. Foundation v3
    F1 freezes that scope. The accepted design revision 6 opens the requested cluster
    and its registered dependants, but does not resolve the scope from the request.

evidence E2:
  |
    The owner clarified that the product function should not be fixed to appearance:
    fixing the scope as a test condition is acceptable, while the function should
    follow the request and the accepted cc304 trial order. The owner instructed
    progress after the distinction and next step were stated. This is direction for
    a candidate, not acceptance of this exact ADR revision.

evidence E3:
  |
    The current POST /api/characters/:id/chat body contains only message. A
    controlledCharacterRevisionCluster appearance option selects the focused route
    in tests; production route construction does not supply it. Existing
    revision-scope replay code is evaluation-only unsealed WIP, not product authority.

premise SCOPE:
  |
    Cc304 plan revision 8 calls for one clear appearance revision through the local
    API or UI, worker, controlled provider driver, persistence and owner review.
    It ends at a non-current candidate and excludes final acceptance, paid calls,
    deployment, create, migration and pointer activation.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    An owner-selected field would move scope interpretation to the user and make
    test control a product interaction. A fixed appearance route would misroute
    other requests. A bounded provider-assisted scope work item preserves the
    message-only interaction but adds one operation, accounting and failure path.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, SCOPE, OPTIONS:
  |
    Propose keeping the ordinary owner message-only request. When focused V3 revise
    is enabled, a bounded provider-assisted scope work item proposes the requested
    semantic cluster from that natural-language message. The server validates the
    proposal within the attempt's bounded accounting, then freezes the resolved
    cluster with the immutable source and request before any character proposal.
    No mandatory owner-facing cluster selector or
    product-wide appearance constant is added. The test may inject appearance as a
    controlled condition, but that cannot prove scope resolution.

decision D2 based_on D1, E1, E3, SCOPE:
  |
    For the first cc304 trial, admit only a clear single-cluster request. If scope
    is ambiguous, invalid, or spans multiple independent clusters, do not guess,
    silently fall back to generic revision, or create a focused candidate. An invalid
    response is a technical failure, not an owner question. Ambiguity may ask the
    owner only under accepted R13 conditions; otherwise it is a bounded failure.
    A multi-cluster request is not handled by this first trial. The exact public
    result shapes are successor design decisions before route wiring; this trial
    does not define eventual complete product behavior for these cases.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, SCOPE:
  |
    Exercise one clear appearance-text request with a local controlled provider
    response through the ordinary owner HTTP command and existing focused worker,
    kernel, adapter, persistence and review diff. Keep the current V3 generation
    and pointer unchanged. The face image, final acceptance and other modes are out
    of this trial. A diagnostic fixed-scope test and unsealed replay results are not
    acceptance evidence for the natural-language step.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-16, after the complete Japanese review scope and exact ADR-0035
    revision 2 were presented with the explicit question whether to accept it,
    the product owner replied: 進めてください. The reviewed source snapshot was
    cf0bc31584850e8d5b08226158a7b18325df011e5a452dac5c30aad1ccfe7c9a.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    Accept ADR-0035 revision 2 exactly as reviewed. This authorizes the local
    cc304 implementation slice within D1-D3 and does not authorize paid provider
    calls, final candidate acceptance, pointer movement, deployment, or release.
